Commit the current changes locally on the current branch.

Description of the changes, if provided: $ARGUMENTS

- Always commit locally on the current branch. Do not push, open a PR, or switch branches unless the user asks.
- If on `main` or `master`, stop and tell the user rather than committing.
- Group related edits into one commit per logical unit of work, so each can be reverted on its own.
- Stage the files for each commit explicitly. Never `git add -A`.
- Use a conventional commit subject: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `chore:`, `test:`, etc. Lowercase, imperative mood, no trailing period, under 72 characters.
- Do not add attribution trailers or session links (no `Co-Authored-By:`, no `Claude-Session:`, no claude.ai/code URLs).
{% if claude_rtk_active %}
- Run each command separately. Never `&&`-chain commands.
{% endif %}
